  "revision": "1. **Fix Silhouette Contrast (Critical):** The dark silhouettes of the dino and cacti currently merge with the dark ground strip. Add a distinct, lighter 'ground line' (a 2-3px stroke in a warm sand color) at the top of the dark ground layer, or add a subtle drop shadow under the entities to ensure they pop against the terrain. \n2. **Unify HUD & Hierarchy:** Group the Score, Best, and Speed metrics into a single, cohesive horizontal bar in the top-right corner to create a clear 'status zone'. Within this bar, make the Speed value slightly larger to emphasize the runner mechanic without breaking the grouping. \n3. **Refine Ground Rhythm:** Replace the random, noisy dashed lines on the ground with a consistent, rhythmic pattern (e.g., evenly spaced pebbles or a clean, repeating geometric texture) to convey speed and 'rhythmic spacing' without visual clutter. \n4. **Integrate Jump Instruction:** Remove the heavy white background from the 'TAP / SPACE' box. Replace it with a semi-transparent dark overlay or a simple outline that matches the modern-retro aesthetic, and reposition it closer to the dino or the bottom of the screen to reduce floating clutter and let the dino remain the primary focal point. \n5. **Enhance Atmospheric Depth:** Add a subtle, warm 'rim light' or gradient at the very top edge of the ground strip to simulate sun reflection, adding depth without lightening the base color and compromising silhouette contrast. Sharpen the sun rays into a consistent geometric starburst and increase the definition of the clouds to match the crispness of the foreground.",
